# Division and remainder: the same-signedness forms, the mixed-signedness
# forms (the divisor is wrapped to the left kind), and their errors.
7 // 2
-7 // 2
7 // -2
-7 // -2
7 % -3
-7 % 3
-7 % -3
7 // 0
7 % 0
7_i8 // 0_u8
7 % 0_i64
100_i8 // 200_u8
200_u8 // -1_i8
7_i8 % 255_u8
-7_i8 % 250_u8
# Not here: `-128_i8 // 255_u8` and `-128_i8 % 255_u8`. The hosted fold wraps the divisor to -1 after its
# overflow check has passed on 255, and then divides MIN by -1 in the machine: arm64 answers MIN and 0,
# x86-64 traps and the hosted compiler dies with SIGFPE. There is no hosted answer to compare with.
-128_i8 // 128_u8
-128_i8 // 255_i16
255_u8 // -1_i8
